        {
            "id": "31849704",
            "user": "Seymour Edits",
            "timestamp": "22:01, 9 August 2023",
            "anon": false,
            "size": "(12,215 bytes)",
            "change": -236,
            "summary": "(Removed and replaced bad sources for wikiHaus content team)",
            "is_minor": false,
            "is_expert": false,
            "status": "active",
            "contribution_type": "sourcing",
            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "#Secure the mounting plate to the interior wall. Hold the mounting plate against the wall where you want to install the indoor unit. [[Use a Level|Use a level]] to make sure it is both horizontally and vertically level. Use a pencil to mark the locations of the screw holes, remove the plate, then [[Drill a Hole in the Wall|drill a hole]] into the wall where each screw will go. [[Image:Install a Split System Air Conditioner Step 2 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Position the outdoor unit away from any heavily trafficked, dusty, or hot areas. Find the hole you drilled through the mounting plate for the interior unit and position the exterior unit within {{convert|50|ft|m}} so the piping and cable can easily be attached.<ref>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hxYrOv5bV9Y</ref> Choose a location with at least {{convert|12|in|cm}} of space surrounding its perimeter to ensure proper functioning. If possible, select a shady location that’s sheltered from the wind in addition to dust and traffic to keep your unit functioning at its best.[[Image:Install a Split System Air Conditioner Step 7 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Secure the outdoor unit on top of the concrete pad. Lay a rubber cushion on top of the pad to minimize vibration, then set the outdoor condenser unit on top of the pad. Secure the unit [[Bolt Into Concrete|to the concrete]] with anchor bolts.<ref>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hxYrOv5bV9Y</ref>[[Image:Install a Split System Air Conditioner Step 9 Version 3.jpg|center]]"
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "#Secure the mounting plate to the interior wall. Hold the mounting plate against the wall where you want to install the indoor unit. [[Use a Level|Use a level]] to make sure it is both horizontally and vertically level. Use a pencil to mark the locations of the screw holes, remove the plate, then [[Drill a Hole in the Wall|drill a hole]] into the wall where each screw will go.<ref>https://www.thisoldhouse.com/how-to/how-to-install-mini-split-air-conditioner</ref>[[Image:Install a Split System Air Conditioner Step 2 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Position the outdoor unit away from any heavily trafficked, dusty, or hot areas. Find the hole you drilled through the mounting plate for the interior unit and position the exterior unit within {{convert|50|ft|m}} so the piping and cable can easily be attached.<ref>https://www.brighthubengineering.com/hvac/45249-indoor-and-outdoor-installation-of-split-air-conditioners-deciding-the-location/</ref> Choose a location with at least {{convert|12|in|cm}} of space surrounding its perimeter to ensure proper functioning. If possible, select a shady location that’s sheltered from the wind in addition to dust and traffic to keep your unit functioning at its best.[[Image:Install a Split System Air Conditioner Step 7 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Secure the outdoor unit on top of the concrete pad. Lay a rubber cushion on top of the pad to minimize vibration, then set the outdoor condenser unit on top of the pad. Secure the unit [[Bolt Into Concrete|to the concrete]] with anchor bolts.<ref>https://www.brighthubengineering.com/hvac/45811-installation-of-the-outdoor-unit-of-split-air-conditioners/</ref>[[Image:Install a Split System Air Conditioner Step 9 Version 3.jpg|center]]"
                ]
            }
        },
