            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "#Secure the mounting plate to the interior wall. Hold the mounting plate against the wall where you want to install the indoor unit. [[Use a Level|Use a level]] to make sure it is both horizontally and vertically level. Use a pencil to mark the locations of the screw holes, remove the plate, then [[Drill a Hole in the Wall|drill a hole]] into the wall where each screw will go.<ref>https://www.thisoldhouse.com/how-to/how-to-install-mini-split-air-conditioner</ref>[[Image:Install a Split System Air Conditioner Step 2 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#*Make sure there are no pipes or [[Find Electrical Wires in a Wall|wires]] behind the wall before drilling or cutting the hole.",
                    "#Secure the outdoor unit on top of the concrete pad. Lay a rubber cushion on top of the pad to minimize vibration, then set the outdoor condenser unit on top of the pad. Secure the unit [[Bolt Into Concrete|to the concrete]] with anchor bolts.<ref>https://www.brighthubengineering.com/hvac/45811-installation-of-the-outdoor-unit-of-split-air-conditioners/</ref>[[Image:Install a Split System Air Conditioner Step 9 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#*If necessary, you can [[Cut-Copper-Pipe|trim the copper pipes]] to eliminate excess.",
                    "#Seal up the [[Cover a Hole in a Wall|hole in the wall]] using expanding polyurethane foam. Spray expanding polyurethane foam into the hole you drilled to feed the cable and piping through the wall. Make sure the hole is completely sealed to prevent hot air or insects from getting through.[[Image:Install a Split System Air Conditioner Step 14 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#*Refer to the instruction manual [[Service an Air Conditioner|if you have any trouble]] operating your new air conditioner."
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "#Secure the mounting plate to the interior wall. Hold the mounting plate against the wall where you want to install the indoor unit. Use a level to make sure it is both horizontally and vertically level. Use a pencil to mark the locations of the screw holes, remove the plate, then drill a hole into the wall where each screw will go.<ref>https://www.thisoldhouse.com/how-to/how-to-install-mini-split-air-conditioner</ref>[[Image:Install a Split System Air Conditioner Step 2 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#*Make sure there are no pipes or wires behind the wall before drilling or cutting the hole.",
                    "#Secure the outdoor unit on top of the concrete pad. Lay a rubber cushion on top of the pad to minimize vibration, then set the outdoor condenser unit on top of the pad. Secure the unit to the concrete with anchor bolts.<ref>https://www.brighthubengineering.com/hvac/45811-installation-of-the-outdoor-unit-of-split-air-conditioners/</ref>[[Image:Install a Split System Air Conditioner Step 9 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
